{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/455378-obfuscate-and-recorded-media","id":455378,"title":"Obfuscate and Recorded Media","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-23T21:42:44-07:00","id":455378,"title":"Obfuscate and Recorded Media","content":"How does Obfuscate deal with recorded media? I just realized Blood and Smoke doesn't cover the topic at all, except for a quick mention in Obfuscate 2.<br /> <br /> I used to believe that so long as Obfuscate was running, all actions are hidden by it and only looking at a recorded thing after Obfuscate was dropped would pierce it. Otherwise a simple half second delay in the video feed (or the natural delay it takes the computer to process the image) would pierce Obfuscate easily.<br /> <br /> One specific instance I'm thinking of. A Vampire uses Oubliette to alter her house from a broken down shack into a very nice, upper middle class house. Someone takes a picture inside the house. A few days later, they upload the picture to facebook. Assuming Oubliette doesn't end in the interim, does the picture show a broken down shake or a very nice, upper middle class house?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 03-24-2015, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T23:34:57-07:00","id":455481,"title":"","content":"If I understand it correctly, it would show an upper middle class house so long as the Oubliette was in effect. <br /> <br /> If &quot;Touch of Shadow&quot; can hide things even in photographs after the vampire stopped using the discipline, then Oubliette can uphold it's illusion in photographs, even if it only lasts as long as it is in effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T02:36:42-07:00","id":455557,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate is mind control. So in your specific way, I think it would be a broken down shack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T07:27:45-07:00","id":455818,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate works by changing the way people perceive the subject, it doesn't change the subject's actual appearance. So in my opinion, the picture would be <i>of</i> a broken down shack, but while Oubliette was still in effect, people looking at the picture would see an upper middle class house.<br /> <br /> Like the recent &quot;the dress&quot; thing. That was objectively a picture of a blue and black dress, but many people (myself included at first) saw a white and gold dress because the brain tries to interpret the information it recieves from the eyes, and makes a lot of assumptions along the way, not all of which are correct. This can cause you to &quot;see&quot; something other than what you're actually looking at.<br /> <br /> So maybe the exposure in the picture is just such that it makes the peeling paint look like adorable wallpaper. Maybe if you looked at the picture again after the power wears off, you'll have a moment of realization where you finally see the content of the picture for what it really is, like I had when I saw the dress as blue and black and then couldn't un-see it again. &quot;How did I not notice the garbage on the floor before? Must have been the angle.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T10:30:24-07:00","id":457038,"title":"","content":"I vote for seeing the illusion. While, for a mortal or hunter game, it would be pretty cool way to track down a vampire, from inside a vampire game I think it would be less than useful.<br /> <br /> We're talking on bordering on Masquerade breach, rendering the power more of a danger. I mean, hells. If its just a recording, and with the amount of digital records going up all the time? Hell, someone looking it up on Google Earth? A security camera put up across the street with neighbors?<br /> <br /> There's so many situations where it can go wrong to the point its just unfeasable if you do the &quot;review footage and see shack.&quot; I really don't think that's the intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-25-2015, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T13:18:40-07:00","id":457248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/455378-obfuscate-and-recorded-media?p=457038#post457038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vote for seeing the illusion. While, for a mortal or hunter game, it would be pretty cool way to track down a vampire, from inside a vampire game I think it would be less than useful.<br /> <br /> We're talking on bordering on Masquerade breach, rendering the power more of a danger. I mean, hells. If its just a recording, and with the amount of digital records going up all the time? Hell, someone looking it up on Google Earth? A security camera put up across the street with neighbors?<br /> <br /> There's so many situations where it can go wrong to the point its just unfeasable if you do the &amp;quot;review footage and see shack.&amp;quot; I really don't think that's the intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think it would be a masquerade risk. Millions of people saw a picture of a dress &quot;change color&quot; and I very much doubt anyone suspected it had anything to do with vampires.<br /> <br /> ...Well, someone probably did, but no one believed them. People's instinct tends to be that there is a rational explanation for most things, and most people are much more likely to think &quot;oh, I didn't notice that last time I looked at this&quot; or &quot;Oh yeah, i forgot that was in the picture&quot; than &quot;something supernatural was going on here.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T14:30:02-07:00","id":457286,"title":"","content":"not to mention if someone official is reviewing it, it might be better to just come up with an explicable answer rather than try to tackle the strange. Your local coroner probably just wants to go home and watch some TV, not attract the ire of things that go bump in the night.<br /> <br /> Saying vampires did it is also probably a good way to lose your job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}